====================================================================================================
 (0) f(depth) FROM THE KERNEL -- the amplitude ladder (a0 cancels; footing remaps physical members)
====================================================================================================
   the deep-MOND CARRIERS carry the signal; the SURVEY-BRIGHT members are adiabatic-shallow:
    a_in/a0 |  f (relational spread) | physical example (a_ex=a0 shell)
       0.05 |                23.39% | UDG sigma~20 Re~3kpc (ELT-only)
       0.15 |                19.68% | diffuse dSph sigma~22 Re~1.2
       0.50 |                11.94% | MaNGA-reachable dE sigma~50 Re~2
       1.00 |                 6.99% | SDSS-floor dE sigma~90 Re~2.5
       3.00 |                 1.90% | SDSS mid-E sigma~150 Re~3
      10.00 |                 0.27% | SDSS bright E sigma~230 Re~4
   -> f DROPS ~50x from carrier (a_in~0.15a0) to bright E (a_in~10a0). The measurable-by-survey
      members are the SHALLOW ones; the deep ones (large f) are faint/diffuse. That anti-
      correlation is the whole power problem -- but N differs by ~100x too, so we must weigh both.

====================================================================================================
 (1) NULL CALIBRATION + continuum-y power constant (frozen estimator; MG truth f=0 -> standard normal)
====================================================================================================
   MG-truth null (N=400, 20k trials): mean z = -0.013, sd = 1.003, P(z>=3) = 0.0015
   continuum-y N_3sigma = C*(noise/(f*D))^2 with C = 118  (two-class-y C~65 matches banked N=1291; continuum is the honest stacked-sample case)

====================================================================================================
 (2) STACKED SDSS SAMPLE -- VDF-weighted population MC (does N~1e5 compensate for tiny per-member f?)
====================================================================================================
   CANONICAL: sigma-complete VDF stack, <f>=3.30%, 24% of members sit at a_in<1.5a0 (diffuse tail).
     STATISTICAL z at N=1e5 = 7.9  (>>3: the N DOES compensate statistically).
     BUT the detected quantity is a slope of amplitude D*<f> ~ 1.2% in ln-sigma.
   ALTERNATE: sigma-complete VDF stack, <f>=4.05%, 35% of members sit at a_in<1.5a0 (diffuse tail).
     STATISTICAL z at N=1e5 = 9.6  (>>3: the N DOES compensate statistically).
     BUT the detected quantity is a slope of amplitude D*<f> ~ 1.4% in ln-sigma.

====================================================================================================
 (3) THE SYSTEMATIC + CONFOUND FLOOR -- why the SDSS stack's z>>3 is a MIRAGE (honest, load-bearing)
====================================================================================================
   SDSS single-fiber sigma systematic floor (aperture+S/N+z bias): 1-5% in ln-sigma
   IFU (MaNGA/SAMI) resolved-sigma systematic floor:               0.3-1.0% in ln-sigma
   tidal/environmental confound C6 (same SIGN + phase-correlated): 2-8% (../sigma_spread/MG_ZERO.md; separable ONLY by radial profile, not amplitude)

   COMPARE the signal slope D*f AGAINST these floors (the signal-to-systematic ratio, NOT stat S/N):
   route                           D*f (signal)    sys floor  C6 confound  signal>floor?
   SDSS stack (bright/mid E)              1.2% 1- 5%     2- 8%           MARGINAL
   MaNGA/SAMI diffuse dE cut              4.4% 0- 1%     2- 8%             CLEARS
   Coma/nearby deep diffuse               5.9% 0- 1%     2- 8%             CLEARS

   READING (both ways): the SDSS stack is NOT statistics-limited -- it is SYSTEMATICS-limited.
   Its ~1% signal slope sits INSIDE the SDSS sigma-systematic floor (1-5%) AND below the C6 tidal
   confound (2-8%) which shares the signal's sign and phase-space correlation. Beating it needs
   sub-0.5% sigma control + the radial-profile separator -- NOT more galaxies. By contrast the IFU
   routes put a ~4% signal ABOVE their (resolved) systematic floor: for them N, not systematics, binds.

